<# Why it exists: a test ignoring SIGINT once held a local build, and with it the nightly orchestrator, for 109 min
   (docs/architecture.md, [stage-limits]). Template comments only here: every project's file carries what is below,
   a company's repository among them. -#>
// A long stage's time limit, in minutes: past it the stage fails naming itself and the limit, so one hung test
// never holds the nightly orchestrator. An abort by hand before the limit stays an abort. The limits: STAGE_LIMITS
// in aisland/services/jenkins.py.
def limited(String stage, int minutes, Closure body) {
    long started = System.currentTimeMillis()
    try {
        timeout(time: minutes, unit: 'MINUTES') {
            body()
        }
    } catch (org.jenkinsci.plugins.workflow.steps.FlowInterruptedException interrupted) {
        if (System.currentTimeMillis() - started < minutes * 60000L) {
            throw interrupted
        }
        error("<[ timed_out_message ]>")
    }
}
